# Chains of Mephistopheles and Laboratory Maniac, as in the scenario beside this one, but Bot1 has Chains apply first to
# Ancestral Recall's first draw from its empty library (CR 616.1): it discards the Forest instead, and so draws a card - a
# draw that Chains does not replace again (CR 614.5) but Laboratory Maniac does, the library still being empty, so Bot1 wins
# the game then (CR 104.2b), with the Forest in its graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Chains of Mephistopheles
Laboratory Maniac
Ancestral Recall
Forest
Plains

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Laboratory Maniac.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Library.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Replace(Chains of Mephistopheles)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)

[Expect]
Result = Bot1 won
Bot2.Status = Lost
Bot1.Hand = Plains
Bot1.Graveyard = Forest; Black Lotus
